# Profile Completion Flow

This rule documents how the application ensures users have at least first and last name set, and how incomplete profiles are prompted to complete their data.

## Problem Addressed

Users could end up with empty `local-user-info` records because:
- OTP login creates a user and a profile with only the `user` relation (no name).
- Existing users logging in via OTP or password were never sent to the "complete profile" step.
- The register-info endpoint did not enforce required fields.

## Backend Validation

**File**: [backend/src/api/auth/controllers/auth.ts](backend/src/api/auth/controllers/auth.ts)

The `registerInfo` handler validates before any DB work:
- `firstName`: required, non-empty string. Returns 400 with message `"نام الزامی است"` if missing.
- `lastName`: required, non-empty string. Returns 400 with message `"نام خانوادگی الزامی است"` if missing.
- `birthDate` and `password` remain optional.

Validation is request-scoped only: it does not modify or overwrite existing user records. Existing users with empty names remain unchanged until they submit the register-info form with names filled in.

## Profile Completeness Check

**File**: [frontend/src/utils/profile.ts](frontend/src/utils/profile.ts)

- `isProfileIncomplete(user: MeResponse): boolean` — returns `true` when `FirstName` or `LastName` is missing or whitespace-only.
- Used by login pages (redirect logic) and by `ProfileCompletionBanner`.

## Login Flow Redirect

When a non-admin user logs in (password or OTP) and their profile is incomplete:
1. After `UserService.me()`, the app checks `!me.isAdmin && isProfileIncomplete(me)`.
2. If true, redirect to `/auth/register/info?phone=...` (and optional `redirect=...` for post-completion).
3. Otherwise, normal redirect (stored redirect URL, `/super-admin`, or `/account`).

**Files**:
- [frontend/src/app/(public)/auth/login/page.tsx](frontend/src/app/(public)/auth/login/page.tsx) — password login
- [frontend/src/app/(public)/auth/login/otp/page.tsx](frontend/src/app/(public)/auth/login/otp/page.tsx) — OTP login

## Register Info Page

**File**: [frontend/src/app/(public)/auth/register/info/page.tsx](frontend/src/app/(public)/auth/register/info/page.tsx)

- Used both for **new users** (after OTP during registration) and **existing users** (redirected from login when profile is incomplete).
- Phone can come from query param `phone` or from `localStorage` key `pendingPhone`.
- **Post-submit redirect**:
  - If query has `redirect` and it is a path starting with `/`, navigate there.
  - Otherwise navigate to `/account` (user is already logged in; no need to send to `/auth/login`).

## Profile Completion Banner

**File**: [frontend/src/components/User/Account/ProfileCompletionBanner.tsx](frontend/src/components/User/Account/ProfileCompletionBanner.tsx)

- Amber/warning banner shown when the current user’s profile is incomplete (`isProfileIncomplete(userData)`).
- Hidden for admins and when profile is complete.
- **Dismissal**: Stored in `sessionStorage` under key `profileCompletionBannerDismissed`; banner reappears in a new session.
- Contains a link "تکمیل اطلاعات" to `/account` and a close button.
- **Placement**: Rendered in [frontend/src/app/(user)/layout.tsx](frontend/src/app/(user)/layout.tsx) above `{children}`, so it appears on all authenticated user pages (account, orders, wallet, addresses, etc.).

## Related Types and Services

- `MeResponse`: [frontend/src/services/user/me.ts](frontend/src/services/user/me.ts) — includes `FirstName`, `LastName`, `Phone`, etc.
- Profile update: PUT `/auth/self` (see [frontend/src/services/user/updateProfile.ts](frontend/src/services/user/updateProfile.ts)).
- Register info API: POST `/auth/register-info` (see [frontend/src/services/auth/register.ts](frontend/src/services/auth/register.ts)).
